<header class="page-header">
        <span class="hero-kicker">How we build trust</span>
        <h1>How We Choose Hospitals</h1>
        <p>Not a single ranking — multiple quality signals, matched to each patient's individual case. Here's what we look at, and what we never do.</p>
    </header>

    <section class="section-shell" style="padding-bottom:36px">
        <h2 class="section-title">Our approach in one line</h2>
        <p class="section-lead">We don't publish a "best hospital" list. We evaluate hospitals across six signals, then match the hospitals that fit your specific condition, timing, budget, and language needs. A great hospital for one case may be the wrong fit for another.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="band">
        <div class="section-shell">
            <h2 class="section-title">The six signals we evaluate</h2>
            <p class="section-lead">Every hospital we recommend must clear multiple bars. One strong signal alone is never enough.</p>
            <div class="signal-grid">
                <div class="signal-card">
                    <div style="font-size:1.8em;margin-bottom:8px">🏥</div>
                    <h3>National Grade 3A</h3>
                    <p>China's highest hospital tier — reserved for tertiary centers with advanced facilities, specialist departments, and the clinical volume to match.</p>
                    <p class="why">Why it matters</p>
                    <p>3A status is a national quality benchmark that signals a hospital is equipped for complex care.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="signal-card">
                    <div style="font-size:1.8em;margin-bottom:8px">🌐</div>
                    <h3>JCI Accreditation</h3>
                    <p>Joint Commission International — the global benchmark for patient safety, clinical quality, and international standards.</p>
                    <p class="why">Why it matters</p>
                    <p>JCI accreditation is independently assessed and focused on patient safety — useful, though not every top Chinese hospital holds it.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="signal-card">
                    <div style="font-size:1.8em;margin-bottom:8px">📊</div>
                    <h3>Specialty Rankings</h3>
                    <p>Cross-referenced: Fudan University, Chinese Academy of Medical Sciences, and discipline-specific national rankings.</p>
                    <p class="why">Why it matters</p>
                    <p>Rankings tell us which departments lead in a given specialty — but we treat them as one input, never the final answer.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="signal-card">
                    <div style="font-size:1.8em;margin-bottom:8px">👨‍⚕️</div>
                    <h3>Surgical Volume</h3>
                    <p>Procedure volume is a useful signal of specialist experience — for example, Fuwai Hospital performs over 15,000 cardiac surgeries a year.</p>
                    <p class="why">Why it matters</p>
                    <p>Higher volume can indicate experience, but volume alone should never determine a hospital or surgeon choice. We weigh it alongside the other signals.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="signal-card">
                    <div style="font-size:1.8em;margin-bottom:8px">🗣️</div>
                    <h3>International Department</h3>
                    <p>English-speaking coordinators, dedicated international patient support, and real experience with cross-border travelers.</p>
                    <p class="why">Why it matters</p>
                    <p>Your ability to communicate and be supported in English is as important as the clinical care itself.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="signal-card">
                    <div style="font-size:1.8em;margin-bottom:8px">💰</div>
                    <h3>Cost Transparency</h3>
                    <p>We work with estimated cost ranges and confirm figures with each hospital before any patient travels.</p>
                    <p class="why">Why it matters</p>
                    <p>No surprise bills. Final pricing depends on diagnosis, materials, length of stay, and hospital assessment.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-shell" style="padding-bottom:36px">
        <h2 class="section-title">How we verify the data</h2>
        <p class="section-lead">Every hospital entry in our directory carries a verification date, and we cross-check details against multiple sources.</p>
        <div class="signal-grid">
            <div class="signal-card">
                <div style="font-size:1.8em;margin-bottom:8px">✅</div>
                <h3>Verification dates</h3>
                <p>Each listing shows when its details were last verified — for example "Verified Apr 2026". Information ages, and we show our work.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="signal-card">
                <div style="font-size:1.8em;margin-bottom:8px">🔁</div>
                <h3>Multi-source cross-checking</h3>
                <p>Names, locations, rankings, and contact details are cross-checked against official hospital websites and public ranking sources.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="signal-card">
                <div style="font-size:1.8em;margin-bottom:8px">⚠️</div>
                <h3>Unverified data is labeled</h3>
                <p>Where we can't confirm a detail, we say so — rather than presenting a guess as fact. If a hospital can't be verified, we don't quietly drop it from our standards.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="band">
        <div class="section-shell">
            <h2 class="section-title">What we don't do</h2>
            <ul class="principle-list">
                <li>We don't take commissions from hospitals — hospitals never pay us to be recommended.</li>
                <li>We don't fabricate hospital or doctor data, rankings, success rates, or international patient numbers.</li>
                <li>We don't present a single "absolute" ranking as the one right answer — fit depends on your case.</li>
                <li>We don't promise treatment outcomes, guarantee hospital acceptance, or guarantee prices or wait times.</li>
                <li>We don't diagnose or replace your doctor's judgment — we help you understand and compare your options.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-shell">
        <div class="final-banner">
            <div>
                <h2>Not sure which hospital fits your case?</h2>
                <p>Start with a free case review — we'll shortlist 2–3 hospitals matched to your condition, timing, and budget.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="final-actions">
                <a href="contact-new.html" class="cta-button">Start Free Case Review</a>
                <a href="pricing.html" class="cta-button alt">View Pricing</a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>
